#: ../../examples/notebooks/10_bench_operation.ipynb:10002
msgid "10. Operating a bench"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/10_bench_operation.ipynb:10004
msgid "The same description of a bench is simulated, then operated, with the digital twin running beside the equipment. The equipment here is the fictitious **LumosLabs** range: its emulators speak the LumosLabs protocol over TCP, so LUMOS drives them exactly as it would drive real devices (same drivers, errors and latencies)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/10_bench_operation.ipynb:10008
msgid "**UC3**: describe a bench (laser, shutter, lens on a stage, camera), record a sequence in simulation, then replay it on the equipment and compare the measured and simulated images;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/10_bench_operation.ipynb:10010
msgid "safety: limits, emergency stop;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/10_bench_operation.ipynb:10011
msgid "**UC4**: calibrate the phase of a photonic chip in operation, against the twin."
msgstr ""

